      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The effectiveness of a wealth tax in reducing inequality is still a subject of debate among economists. Some argue that a well-designed wealth tax, such as a top marginal tax rate of 20-30% or higher, can be an effective way to reduce wealth concentration and inequality by targeting the richest 1% of the population. However, others argue that wealth taxes can distort investment decisions and lead to a brain drain as wealthy individuals may choose to relocate or invest in tax-friendly jurisdictions.",
